 54:PIN 19 = !M32C ;
 55:
 56:M32A.OE = !A22&!A21 ;
 57:     
 58:M32A =
 59:  !A31 & !A23& !A22& !A21& !A20& !A19& !A18              /* 000000-03FFFF 256K */
 60:# !A31 & !A23& !A22& !A21& !A19& !A18& !FA20             /* 000000-03FFFF 256K */
 61:# !A31 & !A23& !A22& !A21& !A20& !A19&  A18&       512K  /* 040000-07FFFF 256K */
 62:# !A31 & !A23& !A22& !A21& !A20&  A19& !A18& !A17& 640K  /* 080000-09FFFF 128K */
 63:# !A31 & !A23& !A22& !A21& !A20&  A19&  A18&  A17& ROM   /* 0E0000-0FFFFF 128K */
 64:# !A31 & !A23& !A22& !A21&  A20&                   1M    /* 100000-1FFFFF 1M */
 65:# !A31 &  A23& !A22& !A21&                         8M;   /* 800000-9FFFFF 2M */
 66:                               
 67:
 68:M32B.OE = A22&!A21 ;
 69:     
 70:M32B =
 71: !A31 & !A23& A22 & !A21&                          8M    /* 400000-5FFFFF 2M */
 72:# A31  & A23 & A22 & !A21& !A20& !A19& !A18& !A17;       /* DIAG 8000000h 128K */
 73:              
 74:
 75:M32C.OE = A21 ;
 76:   
 77:M32C =
 78:  !A31 & A23 & A22 & A21 & A20& !A19&  A18&       !512K  /* F40000-F7FFFF 256K */
 79:# !A31 & A23 & A22 & A21 & A20&  A19& !A18& !A17& !640K  /* F80000-F9FFFF 128K */
 80:# !A31 & A23 & A22 & A21 & A20&  A19& !A18&  A17         /* FA0000-FBFFFF 128K */
 81:# !A31 & A23 & A22 & A21 & A20&  A19&  A18               /* FC0000-FFFFFF 256K */
 82:# !A31 & !A23& A22 & A21 &                         8M    /* 600000-7FFFFF 2M */
 83:# !A31 & !A23& !A22& A21 &                         2M;   /* 200000-3FFFFF 2M */
 84:
 85:/*
 86:DESCRIPTION
 87:This PAL is used in the D4 (386) memomy board to decode addresses within the
 88:memory space and assert the M32* signal. It does all the decoding for all the 
 89:expected options according to the following jumper settings.
 90:
 91:512K 640K                              1M
 92:H    H 256K     000000-03FFFFh         H       NO EXTENDED MEMORY
 93:L    H 512K     000000-07FFFFh         L       1024K   100000-1FFFFFh
 94:L    L 640K     000000-9FFFFFh         
 95:H    L ****     ILLEGAL
 96:8M 2M
 97:H  H   OK
 98:H  L   2048K    200000-3FFFFFh
 99:L  H   6144K    400000-9FFFFFh (NOTE: The 8 Meg board asserts both 8M and 2M
100:L  L  8192K     200000-9FFFFFh strobes)
101:
102:When FA20 is low, the address line A20 should be considered to be low.
103:When FA20 is high, A20 is decoded as usual.
104:
105:The above set of m32 outputs are wire ORed to form the signal M32*. The
106:actual equation for M32 is shown below.
107:M32 = /A31* /A23* /A22* /A21* /A20* /A19* /A18            ;000000-03FFFF 256K

